@* AppChip.razor — shared static pill-shaped tag (CLAUDE.md §3.1), Screen B's
   "نموذج 1" tag next to "لقد اخترت:". Confirmed against
   TaskTwo_from_figma_design.png that this is a purely static label — no
   click/remove affordance anywhere in the reference — so it renders as a
   plain non-interactive <span>, no button/role/focus-ring/touch-target
   machinery (CLAUDE.md §6's interactive-element rules don't apply to a
   non-interactive element; adding them would be interactivity the design
   doesn't have). DOM order (text, then icon) matches the confirmed
   right-to-left reading of the reference under the app's ambient
   dir="rtl" — same "plain DOM order" convention as every other component
   in this library. *@
<span class="app-chip">
    <span class="app-chip__label">@Text</span>
    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Icon))
    {
        <MudIcon Icon="@Icon" Color="Color.Inherit" Class="app-chip__icon" aria-hidden="true" />
    }
</span>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Text { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// Optional leading-in-reading-order (End-position, i.e. rendered after
    /// the text under RTL) icon. Null renders no icon and reserves no gap —
    /// same convention as AppButton's own optional Icon.
    [Parameter] public string? Icon { get; set; }
}
